<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- June 20-22.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- June 20-22.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 films at the June 20-22 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film			 3-day gross   Cumulative gross</p>
<p> 1. Batman &amp; Robin	     $42,872,605	---</p>
<p> 2. My Best Friend's Wedding $21,678,377	----</p>
<p> 3. Con Air			$10,431,513   $67,802,075</p>
<p> 4. The Lost World		$8,039,030  $204,953,959</p>
<p> 5. Speed 2: Cruise Control   $7,436,506   $30,873,832</p>
<p> 6. Austin Powers		 $1,276,103   $48,548,047</p>
<p> 7. Gone Fishin'		  $1,196,170   $16,098,759</p>
<p> 8. Addicted To Love		$901,317   $32,559,560</p>
<p> 9. The Fifth Element	     $865,012   $59,767,649</p>
<p>10. Buddy				 $853,810 $8,974,986</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Batman &amp; Robin&quot; and &quot;Addicted To Love&quot; are released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;My Best Friend's Wedding&quot; is released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.. Sony's Columbia Pictures unit released &quot;Buddy&quot; and &quot;The Fifth Element.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Con Air&quot; and &quot;Gone Fishin'&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co..</p>
<p>&quot;The Lost World: Jurassic Park&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;Speed 2: Cruise Control&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner.</p>
